RF.put("questb:b4",{"7124":{"id":7124,"t":"Capture a Mine","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 1g 80s instead of 0.","obj":"Capture a mine, then return to Corporal Teeka Bloodsnarl in the Alterac Mountains.\nMine Captured","desc":"As battle rages over the landscape of Alterac Valley, so too does it rage through the Coldtooth and Irondeep mines. Both are rich sources of minerals and both are used to store supplies; it's no wonder they are so highly valued!\nHelp our war effort, ‹name›! Capture one of the mines for the Horde! To capture a mine, enter one that we do not control and kill its leader. When that is done, the mine will be ours and we'll send troops to protect it!","rew":"Money: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Frostwolf Clan\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"You haven't yet captured a mine, ‹name›! Find one that we do not control and defeat it's leader!","done":"You captured a mine! With our own warriors protecting it, it will be much simpler to extract minerals from its depths, or gather supplies that have been cached there.\nWell done, ‹name›>. The deed you have done is a great boon to our battle efforts.","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":65.6,"y":55.1,"n":"Corporal Teeka Bloodsnarl","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"644":{"id":644,"t":"Sigil of Trollbane","lv":42,"min":32,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Prince Galen Trollbane and bring the Sigil of Trollbane to Zengu in Hammerfall.\nSigil of Trollbane Prince Galen Trollbane","desc":"The final of the sigils needed to unlock the tomb of Thoras Trollbane is held by his son personally. He resides deep within Stromgarde, in a chapel in the militia-held districts. Prince Galen is well protected and no slouch of a warrior himself, so this task could prove most difficult.","rew":"Money: 55 0 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,450\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"You've returned, ‹name›. Is the line of Ignaeus Trollbane broken?","done":"Quite a day this is, ‹class›. The blood of Trollbane will no longer haunt my people, and the sigils needed to take Trol'kalar are in our possession. Soon, very soon, we will strike against the hated trolls of Zul'Gurub.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.8,"y":34,"n":"Zengu","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"1044":{"id":1044,"t":"Answered Questions","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Thyn'tel Bladeweaver in Darnassus.","desc":"We shall rein in the worgen problem, have no worry of that. This evil that your friend introduced to our woods will be contained, and I bear her no ill will for her actions. Strange events are afoot in these times, ‹name›, and the darkness knows no respite.\nI will keep you no longer. I suspect that there are others that should hear of what you have found in the mines of Duskwood.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nLunaris Bow Moonbeam Wand\nExperience: 3,050\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","done":"So this is the fate of Velinde, is it? The high priestess will be disappointed to hear of this, they were good friends before her disappearance. Still, the Scythe of Elune was surely granted to her as a boon by our goddess, and it is unsettling to me that it has fallen out of her servants' hands.\nAnother matter for another time, however. I owe you my thanks in no small amount for what you have accomplished.\nDuskwood Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":75.3,"y":49,"n":"Jonathan Carevin","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":61.8,"y":39.2,"n":"Thyn'tel Bladeweaver","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"6804":{"id":6804,"t":"Poisoned Water","lv":56,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Aspect of Neptulon on poisoned elementals of Eastern Plaguelands. Bring 12 Discordant Bracers and the Aspect of Neptulon to Duke Hydraxis in Azshara.\n12 Discordant Bracers Discordant Surge\nAspect of Neptulon\nProvided: Aspect of Neptulon","desc":"A force of elemental scouts was sent to the eastern plaguelands of Lordaeron, and the disease of that place twisted and infected them. The Waterlords cannot allow this affront to our purity!\nTake this vial. In it is a quantity of one aspect of Neptulon. If used on the plagued elementals it will fight the poison within their bodies and cure them! But their inner conflict will drive them into a surging madness.\nDefeat the discordant surges and bring me their bracers of binding.","rew":"Experience: 4,350\n+100 reputation with Horde","back":"Do you have the bracers?","done":"You have done well, ‹class›. The corrupted elementals you cured were an outrage to all bodies of water. Our strength lies in our purity and if we are to win our war with the others, we must remain strong.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":79.3,"y":73.7,"n":"Duke Hydraxis","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"724":{"id":724,"t":"Prospect of Faith","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Hammertoe's Amulet to Historian Karnik in Ironforge.\nHammertoe's Amulet Magregan Deepshadow\nProvided: Hammertoe's Amulet","desc":"Okay, okay... who would know what to do?\nHistorian Karnik! That's it!\nHe's in Ironforge. He'll be able to help. He and Hammertoe were workin' together to find the lost artifacts in Uldaman.\nGuess the Shadowforge found out the two of them knew more than they were lettin' on.\nTell Karnik what's happened to Hammertoe and give him the amulet--he'll tell you what needs to be done next.","rew":"Experience: 3,150\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Ah, yes. Another traveler seeking something from the dwarves.\nMa'am, I'm truly sorry, but I've no time to answer meaningless questions right now.","done":"Oh! Well, this is a different matter entirely. You probably don't realize the gravity of this matter yet, do you?\nI care deeply about Hammertoe's demise, but if he sent you here with his amulet, then he understood what's at stake.\nWe will have to take time to mourn his death later.\nLet me show you one of the reasons this amulet is so valuable.\nBadlands Dun Morogh Loch Modan","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":53.4,"y":43.4,"n":"Prospector Ryedol","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.5,"y":23,"n":"Historian Karnik","e":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"6564":{"id":6564,"t":"Allegiance to the Old Gods","lv":22,"min":17,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 1,300 experience instead of 1,750, 0.74 times as much. Read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Bring the Damp Note to Je'neu Sancrea in Ashenvale.\nDamp Note Blackfathom Tide Priestess 33 %\nProvided: Damp Note","desc":"Some poor handwriting is scrawled on the crumpled up note:\n\"Yes, tell all the priestesses to bring the crystals to me. The water elemental spirits are strong within them and they will aid our aquamancers greatly in their own summonings.\nBy controlling the power within the crystals, we will appease Aku'Mai. One day we will have enough power to bring Aku'Mai back to us and the world will return to its greatest era! An era of rule by the Old Gods!\"","rew":"Money: 11 0 gold, 11 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,300\n+75 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Yes, ‹name›? What is it you need? There is still much I must learn about the crystals the naga are gathering.","done":"This is interesting indeed. I am glad you have brought it to my attention.\nNow we have a name for our troubles... Lorgus Jett.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":11.6,"y":34.3,"n":"Je'neu Sancrea","e":1}],"cats":["blackfathom-deeps"]},"4324":{"id":4324,"t":"Yuka Screwspigot","lv":53,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Yuka Screwspigot in the Burning Steppes.","desc":"Although my little brother Ribbly has been worthless his whole life, I think, finally, he has some value! But... we might need your help to capitalize on Ribbly's newfound worth.\nMy sister Yuka has been looking for him for weeks, and tracked him to the Burning Steppes. She sent word to me, asking for some hired hands.\nSo, what do you say? Want to help? If so, then speak with my sister. You'll find her holed up in Flame Crest, a cave northwest of Dreadmaul Rock.","rew":"Experience: 2,650","done":"Yes, I'm looking for my brother. We must find him and retrieve him, bless his heart.\nBut if we can't bring all of him... then his head will suffice.\nTanaris Burning Steppes","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":67,"y":24,"n":"Yorba Screwspigot","s":1},{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":66.1,"y":22,"n":"Yuka Screwspigot","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"7604":{"id":7604,"t":"A Binding Contract","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Turn the Thorium Brotherhood Contract in to Lokhtos Darkbargainer if you would like to receive the plans for Sulfuron.\nThorium Brotherhood Contract\nSulfuron Ingot Golemagg the Incinerator 37 %\nProvided: Thorium Brotherhood Contract","desc":"The undersigned hereby declares that the Sulfuron ingot they are delivering to the Thorium Brotherhood (TB Ltd.) is genuine and not a facsimile thereof. The undersigned also acknowledges that any harm that should come to him/her as a result of attempting to build, forge, find, create, sell, or eat Sulfuras, is not the responsibility or fault of TB Ltd.\nBy signing this contract, you are agreeing to all terms listed herein.\n_________________\nSignature","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Sulfuron Hammer\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Thorium Brotherhood\n+200 reputation with Thorium Brotherhood\n+200 reputation with Thorium Brotherhood\n+200 reputation with Thorium Brotherhood","back":"Do we have a deal?","done":"It has been a pleasure doing business with you, ‹name›!\nOn behalf of TB Ltd., I wish you luck in your search for Sulfuras!\nStart an item: Thorium Brotherhood Contract End Lokhtos Darkbargainer Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 7604","cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"4004":{"id":4004,"t":"The Princess Saved?","lv":60,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Now open to both factions.","obj":"Return to Thrall!","desc":"You have slain my husband, ‹race›! My child will be born into this world without a father.\n<Princess Moira points directly at you.>\nI assure you, this child will be the next ruler of the kingdom of Ironforge. You and your kind shall be hunted down until the end of days for this wrongful act.\n<You think that Princess Moira may be suffering from the residual effect of Thaurissan's spell.>\nLeave me be, ‹race›. I am certain your warchief will be eager to hear the results of his meddling.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nThrall's Resolve Eye of Orgrimmar\nMoney: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Horde","done":"<Thrall is taken aback by the information you have presented to him.>\nA new threat now looms on the horizon. As Magni's years dwindle down, the way shall be opened for this unborn Dark Iron to become ruler of Ironforge.\nYou have accomplished what I asked of you and for that, you shall be rewarded.\nNow leave me, ‹name›! I must confer with Sylvanas and Cairne.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.7,"y":37.8,"n":"Thrall","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"8964":{"id":8964,"t":"Components of Importance","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve a Brilliant Sword of Zealotry and return it to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain.\nBrilliant Sword of Zealotry Scarlet Praetorian","desc":"‹class›, listen closely. Now that we have the brazier, and the means to light it, we still need another component to suffuse it with; something that will provide a focus strong enough to summon the remains of my deceased, former comrades.\nThe siblings, Jarien and Sothos, were believers in the way of the Scarlet Crusade. They aspired to knighthood within that vile organization. Go to Tyr's Hand in Eastern Plaguelands and retrieve a Brilliant Sword of Zealotry from the praetorians there.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"Have you returned already then, ‹class›, with what I sent you out to gather?","done":"A job well done, ‹name›. I will imbue the essence of the sword into the brazier.\nNow all that is left is to get into The Crimson Throne inside The Scarlet Bastion at Stratholme, and use the brazier to summon forth the remains of my former cohorts, Jarien and Sothos. Their souls have been twisted further by their possession of Valthalak's amulet piece and his spirit within.\nBurning Steppes Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":32.3,"y":25.8,"n":"Bodley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-mountain"]},"4724":{"id":4724,"t":"The Pack Mistress","lv":59,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay Halycon, pack mistress of the Bloodaxe worg.\nHalycon slain","desc":"Some say the worg controlled by the Blackrock orcs are the creation of a supernatural force. Others say they are not true worg but instead a breed of demon dog, granted to the orcs by a fallen pit lord.\nThe truth is far less contrived but every bit as frightening. The worg of Blackrock come from Halycon and her mate. Halycon is the gigantic den mother of the worg. Her mate? Nobody has ever lived to tell the tale of that one.\nStrike at the heart of the worg. Destroy Halycon... and ‹name›, watch your back.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nAstoria Robes Traphook Jerkin Jadescale Breastplate\nMoney: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,400\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"With the pack mistress slain, we can begin to thin out the worg sentries of the Spire and eventually make some headway into the city.","done":"Rabid pups? Gizrul the Slavener? And you live to tell the tale?! Incredible! A tribute well earned!","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":6,"y":47.7,"n":"Galamav the Marksman","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"5284":{"id":5284,"t":"The Way of the Weaponsmith","lv":40,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"To become a Weaponsmith, you must make the following items and return them to Ironus: 4 Moonsteel Broadswords, 4 Massive Iron Axes, 2 Heavy Mithril Axes, and 2 Big Black Maces.\n4 Moonsteel Broadsword\n4 Massive Iron Axe\n2 Heavy Mithril Axe\n2 Big Black Mace","desc":"As a weaponsmith you'll find that more often than not, heroes and adventurers will be coming to you for gear. While the workload can be unbearable at times, the riches more than make up for the back strain and ash lung.\nOh yes, ‹name›, weaponsmiths are the ones with all the gold!\nIf you wish to join our ranks, you'll need to show me that you can make me a silver or two - I mean, show me that you've got what it takes to be the go to guy/girl when people need superior quality weapons. Get to work!","rew":"You will learn: Weaponsmith\nExperience: 3,150","back":"<Ironus is busy stacking gold coins into neat little piles.>","done":"About time! I've got customers waiting.\nGive those here and pay attention. You're going to take the first step in your career as a weaponsmith.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.2,"y":28.1,"n":"Ironus Coldsteel","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"4484":{"id":4484,"t":"Libram of Voracity","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -30g instead of 0.","obj":"Black Diamond Borer Beetle 5.2 % , Dark Keeper Uggel 4.6 % , Crest Killer 3.8 % , Burrowing Thundersnout 3.6 % and 4 more\nLibram of Voracity Coldmine Explorer 1.2 % in Alterac Valley , Timbermaw Mystic 0.5 % , Negolash 0.5 % , Dark Keeper Pelver 0.3 % and 4 more\n4 Whipper Root Tuber\n4 Crystal Force","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nLesser Arcanum of Voracity Lesser Arcanum of Voracity Lesser Arcanum of Voracity Lesser Arcanum of Voracity Lesser Arcanum of Voracity","back":"Do not waste my time, ‹race›. Give me what I require. Thirty gold and the components.","done":"My head throbs... The energies of the vast expanses that makes up our universe... ARGGH!\nTake what you desire and leave!","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":65,"y":23.6,"n":"Mathredis Firestar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["burning-steppes"]},"97924":{"id":97924,"t":"Camping 101 skinning","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Helene Peltskinner in Goldshire to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your skinning skill to 20","desc":"Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Camp Chair. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":44.8,"y":63.2,"n":"Sam Sarsaparilla","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":46.2,"y":62.2,"n":"Helene Peltskinner","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94244":{"id":94244,"t":"Craftsmans writ dark leather shoulders","min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Dark Leather Shoulders\nDark Leather Shoulders","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Dark Leather Shoulders, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","back":"Yarr, what business do ye' have with ol' Narkk?","done":"Thar be me shoulderpads, at last!\nEver had one of these squakers perch on your shoulder? Bet ye' haven't! Their claws, they hurt!\nNow they got a place to rest all day, and you have a heavier coinpurse!\n<Narkk eyes said coinpurse.>\nFor now!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":28.2,"y":74.4,"n":"Narkk","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"94324":{"id":94324,"t":"Craftsmans writ distilled firewater","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Distilled Firewater\nDistilled Firewater","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Distilled Firewater, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Distilled Firewater Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94324","cats":["crafting"]},"94004":{"id":94004,"t":"Craftsmans writ elixir of ogres strength","min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Elixir of Ogre's Strength\nElixir of Ogre Strength","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Elixir of Ogre's Strength, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"Wut?","done":"You brought da elixir!!\nT'anks, ‹race›. You come all this way to help Sos'mol. No ogre ever done that before.\nSos'mol will remember this. Pay you back someday. Me promise.","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":38.4,"y":61.3,"n":"Sos'mol","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"3524":{"id":3524,"t":"Washed Ashore","lv":13,"min":11,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Recover Sea Creature Bones from the beached sea creature just south of Auberdine, and then return with it to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.\nSea Creature Bones Beached Sea Creature","desc":"Majestic sea creatures are known to launch themselves at the Darkshore coastline, beached there until they die. Lately, these beasts have been washing ashore in ever-increasing numbers. I've been sent here by the Temple of the Moon to investigate, but the presence of murlocs along the water has made my research difficult.\nThere is a giant creature washed ashore just south of Auberdine that is ringed by the foul Greymist murlocs. Could you go there and retrieve bones from the creature for our study?","rew":"Money: 4 0 gold, 4 silver, 0 copper Experience: 675\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","back":"It is only recently that these creatures started landing on the coast of Darkshore in such alarming numbers. I can't help but think that this is an ill omen of some sort. Recovering a sample of that creature's bones to the south would help us in Darnassus assess this situation!","done":"I hope the murloc did not give you much trouble in collecting this for us! I will be sure to get this on the next hippogryph to Darnassus. The Temple of the Moon has given me some funds to hand out for assistance; please have some with our thanks.\nYour success here emboldens me to offer you a chance to aid the Temple of the Moon further, if you are interested...","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":36.6,"y":45.6,"n":"Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"3764":{"id":3764,"t":"Un'Goro Soil","lv":50,"min":47,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 Un'Goro Soil samples to Jenal at the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus.\n20 Un'Goro Soil Un'Goro Dirt Pile , Gorishi Hive Guard 58.8 % , Gorishi Worker 55.8 % , Gorishi Stinger 55.2 % and 4 more","desc":"The soil of Un'Goro Crater is reportedly enriched with potent magical qualities. I want to know facts from falsehoods; go into the wilds of Un'Goro and acquire enough quality samples of soil for our continued study.\nYou may think that collection tasks are beneath you; that sort of attitude does not endear yourself to me or the Cenarion Circle. Bring the samples to Jenal, who is no doubt wasting time outside behind this tree; just look for the piles of dirt. He will handle the logistics - not I.","rew":"Money: 1 45 1 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,700\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Ah yes, the dirt. The Arch Druid wants twenty loads per adventurer, and twenty loads he shall get. Let those who conspire against us fall to the wayside!","done":"Unload your precious cargo here, noble ‹class›. It must have been quite the burden... not unlike the burden I carry being a visionary. Here is an honorarium for your work, as dictated by the Arch Druid himself.\nArch Druid Staghelm wants to speak with you again ‹name›, but for his next task you will be aided if you have a journeyman's understanding of Herbalism. If you don't know it though, you will still be able to aid the Circle!","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":34.8,"y":9.3,"n":"Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":31.5,"y":8.2,"n":"Jenal","e":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"97284":{"id":97284,"t":"Vahlarriels vengeance","lv":33,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay Burning Blade orcs at Thunder Axe Fortress in the Desolace, then return to Vahlarriel Demonslayer at Nijel's Point.\nBurning Blade Augur slain : 0/ 4\nBurning Blade Reaver slain : 0/ 4\nBurning Blade Adept slain : 0/ 4\nBurning Blade Felsworn slain : 0/ 4","desc":"If Malem is still alive, then I suspect the Burning Blade orcs are expecting someone to come searching for her soon enough. They will certainly be ready for a fight.\nI would prefer if you kept a low profile and stayed out of their way, but the far more likely reality is that they will be looking to meet you, blade to Burning Blade, at every opportunity.\nSo how about we plan to keep score from the start. Kill as many as you can, and I'll make it worth your time.","rew":"Money: 65 0 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,650\nDesolace Open the zone on the world map Level 33 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 31 36 42 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 97284","cats":["desolace"]},"93044":{"id":93044,"t":"A cleansing cry","lv":38,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring Tears of Theradras back to Uthek the Wise in Gelkis Village.\nSpeak with Mulara\n3 Tear of Theradras\nGelkis Clan Centaur","desc":"When you return to Nerlokh in the Valley of Bones, it will not be empty-handed.\nGo inside the cave at the heart of our village and seek out Mulara. Ask for Tears of Theradras on my behalf. Our supply is low, but it is our best hope against the Magram's foul necromancy!\nI will prepare a ritual. We will create a weapon to disrupt their spells.\nLevel 38 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 36 41 48 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 93044\nThe chain\n10 quests from level 32 to 38, 14,740 XP in all.\n1 [ 35 ] Strange Alliance\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Gelkis, then speak with Uthek the Wise.\nCaptain Pentigast Desolace\n2,050 XP\n2 [ 32 ] Raid on the Kolkar\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring 10 Crude Charms to Uthek the Wise in the Gelkis Village in Desolace.\nUthek the Wise Desolace\n2,550 XP\n[ 33 ] Gelkis Alliance\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Gelkis, then speak with Uthek the Wise.\nGurda Wildmane Desolace\n650 XP\n3 [ 35 ] Stealing Supplies\nBring 6 bags of Crudely Dried Meat to Uthek the Wise in the Gelkis Village.\nUthek the Wise Desolace\n1,350 XP\n4 [ 37 ] Ongeku\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring a Draenethyst Shard to Uthek the Wise in the Gelkis Village in Desolace.\nUthek the Wise Desolace\n2,850 XP\n5 [ 38 ] Valley of Bones\nImprove your reputation with the Gelkis, and locate Nerlokh near the Valley of Bones far east of Gelkis Village.\n290 XP\n6 [ 38 ] Ravaging Ravagers\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis Clan and slay 6 Undead Ravagers, then return to Nerlokh at the southern entrance to Valley of Bones.\n1,450 XP\n7 [ 38 ] Facing the Truth\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis Clan, and bring an Accursed Skull and Gelkis Necromantic Garb to Uthek the Wise in Gelkis Village.\n700 XP\n8 [ 38 ] A Cleansing Cry this quest\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring Tears of Theradras back to Uthek the Wise in Gelkis Village.\n2,150 XP\n9 [ 38 ] Test Your Theory\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and dispel the necromantic curse present on the Accursed Skull.\n700 XP","cats":["desolace"]},"5924":{"id":5924,"t":"Heeding the Call","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Mathrengyl Bearwalker in the Cenarion Enclave, Darnassus.","desc":"Excuse me, friend...\nIt has come to my attention that Mathrengyl Bearwalker has put out word that he wishes to speak with you. It seems that your training as a druid is about to take on a new life, and he will be training you personally. Mathrengyl is the direct assistant to the Arch Druid himself, and is one of the most sage and august druids you'll find in Teldrassil.\nHe is located in the Cenarion Enclave of Darnassus, on the second floor of Fandral Staghelm's tree.","rew":"Experience: 85\n+25 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"I am glad you found your way here today. young ‹class›. The time has come for you to take a large step into a much larger world.\nInside each of Cenarius' children is the call to serve nature. Animals and plants are our friends as well as our charges. We choose to devote our lives as preservers of balance for their sakes as well as our own. Your first step into this world will be to learn of the ways of the bear, and to learn strength of body and heart.\nReady yourself!\nDarnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":33.5,"y":8.3,"n":"Fylerian Nightwing","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":35.4,"y":8.4,"n":"Mathrengyl Bearwalker","e":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":36.1,"y":64.4,"n":"Theridran","s":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"98404":{"id":98404,"t":"The great windborne cat spirit","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Recover the Relic of the Fang, Relic of the Claw, and Relic of the Silent Shadow from the Stormrage Barrow Den, and return them to the Avatar of Saeyleenan.\nRelic of the Fang\nRelic of the Claw\nRelic of the Silent Shadow","desc":"In order to draw upon my spirit, you will need to undergo a trail. To understand and respect my form you must prove that you can embody cunning, stealth, and if you should be cornered, ferocity.\nIn the Barrow Dens just east of here, are three relics you must acquire. They are guarded by powerful enraged spirits that will attack you on sight. A statue at the entrance will bless you with temporary stealth to get past them.\nReturn these relics to me to pass the druidic trial of these lands.","back":"Ah, you have returned. I do hope you have brought the relics with you?","done":"Excellent. You have shown you understand the true nature of the cat, and are able to embody the cunning, stealth, and ferocity needed to take my shape.\nI now deem you worthy of my blessing, young ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":44,"y":73.4,"n":"Avatar of Saeyleenan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"3364":{"id":3364,"t":"Scalding Mornbrew Delivery","lv":5,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take a Scalding Mornbrew to Durnan Furcutter inside Anvilmar before it gets cold in five minutes!\nDurnan's Scalding Mornbrew\nProvided: Durnan's Scalding Mornbrew","desc":"Gah! I was supposed to get this delicious scalding mornbrew to Durnan Furcutter inside Anvilmar a while ago now, but I had to deliver one to Grelin here first. I'll never make it to Anvilmar before the brew runs cold!\nYou look fast. Maybe you can make it. This cup will only stay hot for five more minutes, and Durnan didn't order \"chilly\" mornbrew, so get going. Anvilmar is to the northeast, a settlement dug into the mountain.\nThanks, ‹name›, and don't forget to bring me back my mug!","rew":"Experience: 230\n+50 reputation with Ironforge\n+50 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Aye, I'm Durnan Furcutter. You have something for me?","done":"Ah good, now this will hit the spot. Allow me to take a small break while I enjoy this scalding mornbrew!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":25,"y":76,"n":"Nori Pridedrift","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":28.8,"y":66.4,"n":"Durnan Furcutter","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"804":{"id":804,"t":"Sarkoth","lv":5,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the news of Hana'zua's plight to Gornek at the Den.","desc":"Seeing the deed you have done for me steels my heart. I cannot fall so easily! I must endure!\nBut it remains that I cannot make the trek back to the Den unassisted. Please, ‹name›, return to the Den and tell Gornek of my situation. Perhaps he can help me.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSoft Wool Vest Battleworn Chain Leggings\nExperience: 110\n+25 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+25 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","done":"From your description of the beast, I believe you must be speaking of Sarkoth! It is no wonder that Hana'zua was overtaken by it. Aid will be dispatched to him immediately, trouble yourself no more with Hana'zua's plight.\nHowever, I must say, I am most impressed to hear that you brought Sarkoth to death. It is a feat to be proud of, ‹name›. And that you would fight for a stranger's honor, while other tasks occupied your time, your own honor is heightened.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":40.6,"y":62.6,"n":"Hana'zua","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":42.1,"y":68.3,"n":"Gornek","e":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"164":{"id":164,"t":"Deliveries to Sven","lv":23,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the supplies to Sven.\nSupplies for Sven\nProvided: Supplies for Sven","desc":"Do you know Sven? Now, there is a man who does the work of the Light! He and his followers keep a camp at the northwestern edge of Duskwood.\nUnfortunately, because they are so few, they cannot even spare a man to fetch supplies from town. Will you deliver these supplies to him?","rew":"Money: 8 0 gold, 8 silver, 0 copper Experience: 925\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"You look a sturdy type, ‹class›. Have you come to join our fight?","done":"These supplies will be most useful. The aid of the Carevin family is always appreciated. Here is a little something for your trouble.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":75.3,"y":48.7,"n":"Elaine Carevin","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":7.8,"y":34.1,"n":"Sven Yorgen","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"324":{"id":324,"t":"The Lost Ingots","lv":29,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gather 5 Lightforge Ingots, then return to Glorin Steelbrow in the Wetlands.\n5 Lightforge Ingot Bluegill Raider 80 %","desc":"Having grabbed the single lightforge ingot from the waterlogged chest, it is clear that murlocs have stolen the rest. Hunt the murloc raiders near the Flying Osprey wreckage for the lost lightforge iron.","rew":"Experience: 1,750\n+75 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Did you find the lightforge iron you need?","done":"Ah, you found them! Now let's get this lightforge iron hammered into something useful, eh?","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":12.1,"y":64.2,"n":"Waterlogged Chest","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":10.6,"y":60.6,"n":"Glorin Steelbrow","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"1284":{"id":1284,"t":"Suspicious Hoofprints","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Report about the suspicious prints at the Shady Rest Inn to Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore.","desc":"Rows of hoofprints lead away from the still-smoking skeleton of the Shady Rest Inn. There are at least a few visible impressions, with more rows of prints almost imperceptible in the soft mud of the marsh.","rew":"Experience: 1,350","done":"Hoofprints, eh? It is true that there is an extraordinary amount of centaur activity in the lands near the Dustwallow Marsh. In brief excursions into the Barrens, we found their camps and holdings dotting the area.\nI'll send out Falgran Hastil, one of our trackers, to see if he can find where the tracks lead.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":29.7,"y":47.6,"n":"Suspicious Hoofprint","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":68.2,"y":48.6,"n":"Captain Garran Vimes","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"1204":{"id":1204,"t":"Mudrock Soup and Bugs","lv":38,"min":33,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Forked Mudrock Tongues to Morgan Stern in Theramore.\n8 Forked Mudrock Tongue Mudrock Tortoise 25 % , Mudrock Spikeshell 25 % , Mudrock Burrower 25 % , Mudrock Borer 25 % and 1 more","desc":"I'm working on a dish I call \"Mudrock Soup and Bugs.\" I still need the major ingredients, and... well, I don't think I'd last long trudging through Dustwallow Marsh!\nSo, ‹name›, can you do some hunting for me? First, I need the tongues of Mudrock turtles. You can find Mudrocks along the coast, mostly around the bay.\nBut I don't want just any tongues! I hear that the tongues of some Mudrocks are forked...\nThey say the forked tongues have a distinct flavor, and I want that flavor in my dish...","rew":"Experience: 2,850\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Did you get the forked tongues?","done":"These will do fine! Thank you, ‹name›!\nNow I'll try different cooking techniques on these tongues to find the best way to bring out their flavor.\nEventually I'll have a dish worthy of serving at the Blue Recluse in Stormwind!","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":66.3,"y":45.5,"n":"Morgan Stern","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"6164":{"id":6164,"t":"Augustus' Receipt Book","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Augustus' Receipt Book to Augustus the Touched in Terrordale.\nAugustus' Receipt Book Augustus' Receipt Book","desc":"I'm ready for business! What you do want?\nOh wait... I can't open up shop without my receipt book. How am I to keep track of things without my receipt book?\nI must have left it in town somewhere. I had a room in the inn... the book must be there.\nBring me my book. Please, bring it to me! Bring me my book and you'll see! I'll set up shop and you'll see that my prices are INSANE!","rew":"Experience: 1,400","back":"Do you have my receipt book? I can't wait to get back to business!","done":"There it is! And oh my! I forgot how full it was!\nThis is a glorious day, ‹name›! Stupendous! Insanely good, I say!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":11.4,"y":26.4,"n":"Augustus the Touched","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9204":{"id":9204,"t":"Craftsman's Writ - Stonescale Eel","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver 40 Stonescale Eel and the Craftsman's Writ - Stonescale Eel - to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nCraftsman's Writ - Stonescale Eel\n40 Stonescale Eel\nProvided: Craftsman's Writ - Stonescale Eel","desc":"The bearer of this writ is entitled to payment in the form of an insignia of their choice upon completion of the contracted work order.\nWork Order FS-5:\n40 Stonescale Eel.\nAll filled orders should be delivered to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nContract is null and void if tampered with or damaged.\n-Dispatch Commander Metz, The Argent Dawn","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Crusade Insignia of the Dawn\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Filling a work order, ‹class›?","done":"You could have used this for something else, but you didn't, did you? No use crying about it now, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.7,"y":48.5,"n":"Packmaster Stonebruiser","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9124":{"id":9124,"t":"Cryptstalker Armor Doesn't Make Itself...","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Huntsman Leopold at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 30 Crypt Fiend Parts.\n30 Crypt Fiend Parts Nerubian Overseer , Necrofiend 79.1 % in Scholomance , Crypt Crawler 69.6 % in Stratholme , Crypt Beast 69.5 % in Stratholme and 4 more","desc":"How would you like to earn yourself one of these shiny coins?\n<Leopold holds up an insignia of the Crusade.>\nI've got a little problem that you might be able to help me with, ‹name›. You see, I make Cryptstalker armor for those daft enough to venture into Naxxramas. While they supply me with the core material requirements for the armor, I always run out of the crypt fiend parts. Bring me back a bundle of parts and I'll pay you with an insignia - usable at the quartermaster.","rew":"You will receive:\nInsignia of the Crusade\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"How goes the hunt?","done":"Ah, that'll do nicely, ‹name›. Remember, I'm always accepting more parts. For every bundle you bring me, I'll reward you with an insignia.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.9,"n":"Huntsman Leopold","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"84":{"id":84,"t":"Back to Billy","lv":6,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Pork Belly Pie to Billy Maclure at the Maclure Vineyards.\nPork Belly Pie\nProvided: Pork Belly Pie","desc":"Here you go. And when you give this pie to that Billy, you tell him I hope he chokes on it!","rew":"Experience: 140\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Ugh... I'm starving! Do you have that pie for me, ‹name›?","done":"Mm, yum! This pie is the best!\nI think my memory is coming back to me...","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":34.5,"y":84.3,"n":"\"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.1,"y":85.7,"n":"Billy Maclure","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"5204":{"id":5204,"t":"Retribution of the Light","lv":57,"min":49,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Jaedenar and kill the succubus Rakaiah before finding the Remains of Trey Lightforge.\nRakaiah slain","desc":"She would like to pretend that she's fine. She'd love for me to think that she's strong enough to deal with all of this on her own, but I know better than that. Trey's death and hearing the torture he was put through is going to haunt her for a long time, and there's nothing we can do to stop that. But we can give her some peace!\n‹name›, return to Shadow Hold, kill Trey's torturer and find his remains. There is no reason we can't tie off all these loose ends while Arko'narin mourns in her own private way.","rew":"You will receive:\nRemains of Trey Lightforge\nExperience: 4,500","back":"You inspect the body, and there is no doubt that these are the remains of the Knight of the Silver Hand, Trey Lightforge. For a moment you think of Arko'narin and question if anyone in your life meant as much to you as this man meant to the Night elf captive you recently helped escape Shadow Hold.\nAfter taking another moment to gather your thoughts, you know that you cannot take the paladin's remains back to Jessir without killing his torturer first.","done":"You gather the paladin's remains as carefully as you can, recalling that at least his spirit has been released from any pain or suffering that might have been forced upon him.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":51.3,"y":82,"n":"Jessir Moonbow","s":1},{"z":"Felwood","x":38.5,"y":50.4,"n":"Remains of Trey Lightforge","e":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"8484":{"id":8484,"t":"The Brokering of Peace","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Timbermaw Offering of Peace to King Magni Bronzebeard in Ironforge.\nTimbermaw Offering of Peace\nReach 42000 reputation with Timbermaw Hold\nProvided: Timbermaw Offering of Peace","desc":"Your deeds go beyond the tale of a simple hero, ‹name›. If you are a representative of your people, then your people are ones we would work to make peace with.\nPlease - take this offering to the dwarven king that resides in a mountain of iron; I believe you call this city Ironforge. In times past, he had tried to make contact with us on behalf of his Alliance. It is now only fitting to acknowledge you as the key in your Alliance's efforts in brokering peace.","rew":"Experience: 9,950","back":"‹class›, you are welcomed in my domain. Ironforge should always be considered a home to a hero such as yourself. Now, what business do you have with me?","done":"Indeed, this is a most fortuitous turn of events. Were a lasting peace to be made with these creatures, this would certainly give us an advantage in the affairs of Kalimdor... one that the Night Elves cannot support on their own. I will notify the other leaders of the Alliance of this immediately, and further diplomats will be dispatched!\nAs for you, ‹name›... you have shown courage in both diplomacy and in action. I thank you, as does the whole of the Alliance.\nFelwood Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":65.2,"y":2.7,"n":"Gorn One Eye","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":57.4,"y":30.1,"n":"King Magni Bronzebeard","e":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"3124":{"id":3124,"t":"Hippogryph Muisek","lv":47,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 10 Frayfeather Hippogryphs of any type, then use the Muisek Vessel to shrink and capture them.\n10 Hippogryph Muisek\nHippogryph Muisek Vessel\nProvided: Hippogryph Muisek Vessel","desc":"Since you have proven that you are both trustworthy and gifted with the ability to use the muisek vessel, I now wish you to capture another creature.\nHippogryphs have been loyal companions to the night elves for many years; their spirits are loyal and steadfast.\nYour task is to kill 10 frayfeather hippogryphs, and quickly, shrink and capture them with the vessel, so that their muisek may be preserved. You will find the hippogryphs in the High Wilderness, to the south of here.","rew":"Experience: 4,200\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Were you able to capture the hippogryphs?","done":"After killing an animal, if we allowed the muisek to escape, it may take the form of an even greater creature. We would never be safe from its vengeance.\nThis is a dangerous job I have given you, ‹name›. Again, you have completed it well.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.4,"y":43.4,"n":"Witch Doctor Uzer'i","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"564":{"id":564,"t":"Costly Menace","lv":34,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Darren Malvew of Southshore wants you to kill 8 Mountain Lions and 10 Hulking Mountain Lions.\nMountain Lion slain : 0/ 8\nHulking Mountain Lion slain : 0/ 10","desc":"Ain't nothin' that irks me more than losin' these here beautiful horses. And believe me, we've lost quite a few between them pesky undead creeps, the dang Syndicate gang and all the other good-for-nothin' scoundrels pokin' about these parts.\nBut I swear on my ol' grand-daddy's grave there ain't no bigger menace to our horses here than them Mountain Lions up in Alterac. Always comin' down from the hills and makin' my life difficult!\nYou fancy yourself a hero? Go and do somethin' about it then!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nShepherd's Girdle Shepherd's Gloves\nYou will also receive:\nRecipe: Tasty Lion Steak 5 Tasty Lion Steak\nExperience: 2,700\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Mountain Lions killin' off our horses left and right and here you are wantin' to jibber-jabber about the weather and what not.\nOught to go and find myself a real hero. More killin' and less talkin'.","done":"Ain't that great news! Should-a gone and found me a regular ol' war hero from day one to take care of them beasts. You'd-a made your pappy proud, ‹name›.\nHillsbrad Foothills Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":52.4,"y":56,"n":"Darren Malvew","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"6084":{"id":6084,"t":"Taming the Beast","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Taming Rod to tame a Snow Leopard. Practice your skills, then return to Grif Wildheart in Kharanos.\nTaming Rod\nProvided: Taming Rod","desc":"Those crag boars are quite burly; maybe you'd like something with a little more finesse? Alright then, I've got jus' the thing. South and east of here, you'll find large white cats called snow leopards. Just like an elegantly-carved rifle, behind their beautiful exterior lies a powerful fighter, capable of doing extreme damage. You'll find them to be much more agile an' swift than the boar you tamed.\nTake this taming rod and see how you like the snow leopard.","rew":"Experience: 850","back":"What do you think of the snow leopard, ‹name›?","done":"When I feel you've learned enough, I will grant you the ability to choose any pet of your liking.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":45.8,"y":53,"n":"Grif Wildheart","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"2964":{"id":2964,"t":"A Future Task","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with High Explorer Magellas in Ironforge.","desc":"Well ‹name›... we seem to be at a temporary dead end here. We know what we need - the Plates of Uldum - but we have no idea where they might be. We'll need to do quite a bit of research on this to come up with a solid plan of attack. I have a couple ideas where to start looking; I have high hopes that soon, we'll be asking you to head out and recover them.\nThe High Explorer needs to be informed on this, ‹name›; no doubt, he also wants to thank you personally for once again aiding the League.","rew":"Money: 2 20 2 gold, 20 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,700\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","done":"We're all in agreement then - the best plan of attack is putting this on hold until we can narrow down the areas where these plates might lie hidden. You've brought us this far ‹name›, and I hope you will be the one to head back in to the field to unlock Uldum for us all!\nAllow me to give you this honorarium in the meantime; this should cover any expenses you've encountered in assisting us, and a little something extra. Be sure to check back with us soon... Uldum beckons!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.5,"y":23,"n":"Historian Karnik","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":24.1,"n":"High Explorer Magellas","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8724":{"id":8724,"t":"Morningdew the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"The heavens, in their countless stars, hold answers to earthly mysteries, ‹name›. Might, then, the wise, and the lucky, gaze up and find truth?","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":79.7,"y":77.3,"n":"Elder Morningdew","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"8644":{"id":8644,"t":"Stonefort the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"It is good to know the people of this land still pay homage to the olden races. I bid you well, ‹name›, and offer you this token...\nStart Elder Stonefort End Elder Stonefort Level 60 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 56 58 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 8644","cats":["lunar-festival"]},"9364":{"id":9364,"t":"Fragmented Magic","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Polymorph the Spitelash of Azshara and kill the clones that appear several seconds later. When you have slain 50 Polymorph Clones, return to Archmage Xylem in Azshara.\nPrismatic Shell Warlord Krellian\nPolymorph Clone slain : 0/ 50\nProvided: Prismatic Shell","desc":"My research has revealed a unique purpose for the prismatic shell.\nCarry the shell and cast your polymorph spell on the Spitelash in Azshara. If you wait a few moments, the chaotic aura of the shell will cause them to split into several smaller clones for a few moments. Kill these clones as quickly as possible, and the shell will collect their essence.\nWhen the shell is full, return it to me.","rew":"You will learn: Polymorph\nExperience: 6,600","back":"Have you collected the magic?","done":"Splendid! Splendid!\nNow we are able to reform this magic into a new spell. Behold!","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":29.2,"y":40.2,"n":"Archmage Xylem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"7044":{"id":7044,"t":"Legends of Maraudon","lv":49,"min":41,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Recover the two parts of the Scepter of Celebras: the Celebrian Rod and the Celebrian Diamond.\nFind a way to speak with Celebras.\nCelebrian Diamond Lord Vyletongue\nCelebrian Rod Noxxion","desc":"A dark satyr called Lord Vyletongue spread his evil through these twisting caves, poisoning the minds of all inside. He still resides beyond the purple crystals.\nVyletongue also created a living symbol of his corruption called Noxxion that dwells beyond the orange crystals. Together, they have stolen the two parts of my brother's scepter. Celebras, my brother... he wanders blindly inside, cursed by corruption.\nYou must help him! Find the pieces, and speak to my brother... somehow.","rew":"Experience: 3,400","back":"I have awoken from a nightmare that seemed it would never end...","done":"Now that you have recovered the two parts of my scepter, I have hope that Maraudon may one day be rid of the Vyle corruption.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":32.1,"y":64,"n":"Cavindra","s":1}],"cats":["maraudon"]},"6644":{"id":6644,"t":"Favor Amongst the Brotherhood, Lava Core","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Lava Core Lava Elemental 23.8 % , Lava Reaver 22.1 % , Molten Destroyer 15.4 % , Golemagg the Incinerator 14 % and 3 more","back":"The Thorium Brotherhood sympathizes with your plight, ‹race›. This is why Lokthos has been empowered to bargain.\nOffer 1 Lava Core and you shall be granted favor amongst the Brotherhood.","done":"Your offering has been accepted. Favor you have gained. Continue and you shall be allowed access to the ancient trades.\nStart Lokhtos Darkbargainer End Lokhtos Darkbargainer Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 6644","cats":["molten-core"]},"1124":{"id":1124,"t":"Wasteland","lv":55,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Layo Starstrike near the Valor's Rest graveyard of Silithus, showing him Rabine's Letter.\nRabine's Letter\nProvided: Rabine's Letter","desc":"West of Un'Goro Crater, via the northwestern ridge, is a harsh wasteland - Silithus. Few know that an ancient war was waged there between the night elves and a malign, alien power. The evil was sealed, but now we suspect that forces work to stir this... unspeakable horror.\nSeek out Layo Starstrike, one of our agents in Silithus; look for him at Valor's Rest, the final resting spot for the fallen of the wastes. Give him this letter, and he will give you his trust accordingly.","rew":"Experience: 2,800\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"This is a dangerous land to be so casual, ‹class›. What brings you to the wastes of Silithus?","done":"Rabine sent you, did he? Well, consider yourself welcomed here... as much as this desolate and forsaken land can welcome someone.\nI wasn't alive during the time of the great tribulations that took place here, but there are parts of this desert that might as well be eerie pictures of that forgotten past. With your help, the Cenarion Circle might be able to bring finality to a threat that was supposed to have died generations ago.\nMoonglade Silithus","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":51.7,"y":45.1,"n":"Rabine Saturna","s":1},{"z":"Silithus","x":81.9,"y":18.9,"n":"Layo Starstrike","e":1}],"cats":["moonglade"]},"5844":{"id":5844,"t":"Welcome!","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Camp Narache Gift Voucher to Vorn Skyseer.\nCamp Narache Gift Voucher\nProvided: Camp Narache Gift Voucher","desc":"Welcome to the World of Warcraft!\nAs special thanks for purchasing the World of Warcraft Collector's Edition, turn in this gift voucher to Vorn Skyseer in Camp Narache. You'll then be given a gift: a little companion to join you on your quest for adventure and glory.\nThanks again, and enjoy your stay in the World of Warcraft!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDiablo Stone Panda Collar Zergling Leash","back":"Greetings! It is a pleasure to meet you!\nI see you have a special voucher. Give it to me and I will offer you something in exchange.","done":"You are indeed a special hero, ‹name›. We welcome you to the world of Azeroth, and offer you one of these unique gifts!","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":44.1,"y":77.4,"n":"Vorn Skyseer","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9044":{"id":9044,"t":"Redemption Legguards","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Commander Eligor Dawnbringer at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a pair of Redemption Legguards if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Legguards, 20 Wartorn Plate Scraps, 4 Arcanite Bars and 2 Nexus Crystals.\nDesecrated Legguards\n20 Wartorn Plate Scrap Infectious Ghoul 22.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 21.6 % in Naxxramas , Plagued Deathhound 21.3 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 20.8 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n4 Arcanite Bar\n2 Nexus Crystal","desc":"You will find the remnants of our fallen heroes on the corpses of the Lords of Naxxramas. Bring those desecrated keepsakes to me along with wartorn plate scraps and crafting materials capable of revitalizing the cursed armor and I shall craft a fine piece of armor for you.","rew":"You will receive:\nRedemption Legguards\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Redemption Legguards.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.6,"n":"Commander Eligor Dawnbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"244":{"id":244,"t":"Encroaching Gnolls","lv":16,"min":11,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Report to Deputy Feldon.","desc":"Hail, ‹class›. I am charged to patrol this stretch of road. Although the road is safe for now, I've seen gnoll encampments to the north and east of here.\nLakeshire must know of the gathering gnoll force! Report to Deputy Feldon in Lakeshire and tell him of the gnolls. Do this, and I'm sure Feldon will offer you a scout's wage.\nFeldon's usually inspecting the area south of the bridge to Lakeshire.","rew":"Money: 2 0 gold, 2 silver, 0 copper Experience: 290\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","done":"There are Redridge gnolls that close to Elwynn?? They may be poised to advance into our homeland. Soon the people of Lakeshire may not be the only humans under siege!\nHere is your pay, though you bring us dire news. And it comes at a bad time, for we are ill equipped to deal with it.","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":10.2,"y":71.5,"n":"Guard Parker","s":1},{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":25.6,"y":60,"n":"Deputy Feldon","e":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"95204":{"id":95204,"t":"Crest of lordaeron","lv":22,"min":16,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Bring the Crest of Lordaeron to Oran Snakewrithe in Undercity.\nProvided: Crest of Lordaeron","desc":"<A weathered crest depicting the mark of Lordaeron. With so few relics left after the kingdom's fall, someone in the Undercity would be very keen to get their hands on this.>","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSmall Sack of Gems\nExperience: 5,450","back":"What have you got there, ‹class›? A tasty morsel?","done":"<Oran bites the crest to ensure authenticity.>\nWell I'll be. A genuine relic of our home. Mostly intact, too. We need to be extra careful with this one.\nThank you for your aid in restoring our history, ‹class›. I'll see to it that we take good care of this.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":73.4,"y":32.4,"n":"Oran Snakewrithe","e":1}],"cats":["ruins-of-lordaeron-dungeon"]},"6964":{"id":6964,"t":"The Reason for the Season","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Sagorne Creststrider in the Valley of Wisdom of Orgrimmar about the Feast of Winter Veil.","desc":"Gifts, treats, presents... bah, I say!\nThose goblins pollute the true meaning of this season - the Feast of Winter Veil. This is a time of renewal; the land slumbers under a blanket of snow brought forth by Greatfather Winter, who is NOT the bumbling fool over there in the red suit!\nIf you're interested in learning what the Feast is all about for yourself, ask Sagorne Creststrider. I'm sure he'll be surprised that someone cares about history rather than getting presents.","rew":"Experience: 650","done":"The Feast of Winter Veil, you say? Alas, in times past it held a more substantial meaning to us tauren. Nowadays, it seems as though others have turned the legend of this season of renewal into something that helps to sell candies and presents.\nIt's no surprise that Furmund is bitter about that sort of change. He and other tauren like him cling to our past like a banner of war. While I think a little celebration is always good, it is important to remember the origins of the Feast.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":50.9,"y":65.3,"n":"Furmund","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":38.7,"y":35.9,"n":"Sagorne Creststrider","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"92484":{"id":92484,"t":"Embracing the elements","lv":2,"min":2,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Examine the Humming Recall Crystal then speak with Windshaper Boro in Thendal Grove.\nProvided: Humming Recall Crystal","desc":"While you were away dealing with our vuldren problem, our resident Shaman trainer--Windshaper Boro--left this recall crystal for you. Please examine it, then speak with Boro just over yonder near the center of the village.","back":"Winds guide you, ‹name›.","done":"Can you hear it? The whispers of the winds? Doubtful, considering that the spirits stopped speaking with us when they left us those years ago.\nThose among us who would seek audience with the spirits of the four winds once more hone our understanding of the elements and the natural world, dearly hoping to reestablish the dialogue that was so abruptly ended.\nWould you walk this path and master the elements?\nSpeak with me again if you wish to take your next steps and I will train you.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42,"y":23.4,"n":"Rorian the Dayseeker","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42.7,"y":23.5,"n":"Windshaper Boro","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"1524":{"id":1524,"t":"Call of Fire","lv":11,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Torch of the Dormant Flame to Telf Joolam in Durotar.\nTorch of the Dormant Flame\nProvided: Torch of the Dormant Flame","desc":"You are powerful enough to wield the totem of fire, but that does not mean you are ready.\nAlong the Southfury River in Durotar, before the Great Sea, lies a hidden trail to one of the highest peaks in the land. Find your way to the top and you shall find one of our holy shrines watched over by Telf Joolam--the Shrine of the Dormant Flame.\nTake this torch to him--it marks that you attempt to tame fire. Return it to me aflame by the brazier at the shrine and I will see you are given the totem of fire.","rew":"Experience: 650","back":"Greetin's, ‹name›. You've found yerself at the Shrine of the Dormant Flame. Only those knowledgeable enough in the shamanistic arts will ever learn the secrets of this place and the power it holds. I'm sorry you made the trip all this way, only to be turned back now--the journey up here is far from safe after all--but I am the keeper of the shrine, and I cannot allow just anyone to wander around here.","done":"Ah, my mistake, ‹name›. I apologize. I did not realize you possessed the Torch. I am pleased to make your acquaintance.\nMany adventurers find their way here while looking for lost treasure or the promise of mystical creatures to slay, only to be turned away from a seemingly empty shrine. But we know the truth, do we not, ‹name›?\nThis shrine holds a greater secret from the mundane members of the Horde. To us, it is sacred.\nThe Barrens Durotar","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":56,"y":19.9,"n":"Kranal Fiss","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":38.6,"y":59,"n":"Telf Joolam","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8324":{"id":8324,"t":"Still Believing","lv":59,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Encrypted Twilight Text Twilight Prophet , Twilight Marauder 25 % , Twilight Marauder Morna 25 % , Twilight Overlord 25 % and 4 more","rew":"Money: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper","back":"Find any more encrypted texts? Bring me a good batch of them, this decoding work takes some time.","done":"Excellent! I can't wait to read these. Please do keep bringing the encrypted texts here if you find them.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":67.2,"y":69.8,"n":"Hermit Ortell","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8804":{"id":8804,"t":"Desert Survival Kits","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 60 instead of 55.","obj":"Bring 4 Globes of Water, 4 Powerful Anti-Venom and 4 Smoked Desert Dumplings to Calandrath at the inn in Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing I in order to complete this quest.\n4 Globe of Water Princess Tempestria 77.1 % , Lord Skwol 47.6 % , Hydrospawn 20 % , Muck Splash 16.1 % and 4 more\n4 Powerful Anti-Venom\n4 Smoked Desert Dumplings\nLogistics Task Briefing I\nProvided: Logistics Task Briefing I","desc":"With the arrival of fresh recruits to Cenarion Hold comes the problem of keeping them alive in the desert. Dehydration as well as numerous poisonous creatures present a serious threat to inexperienced volunteers. Gather the supplies necessary for a desert survival kit and bring them to Calandrath in Cenarion Hold.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Logistics Badge Logistics Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.9,"y":39.2,"n":"Calandrath","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"6324":{"id":6324,"t":"Return to Podrig","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Buy a bat ride to the Sepulcher from the bat master Michael Garrett, then bring Gordon's Crate to Deathguard Podrig in the Sepulcher.\nGordon's Crate\nProvided: Gordon's Crate","desc":"The bat master in the Sepulcher is Karos Razok. If you have already met him, then I can give you a bat to fly back to him.\nOur bats will always fly to the Undercity, but to travel to more remote locales their rider must first visit the area and speak with its bat master.\nYou have met Karos in the Sepulcher, so you may now fly bats there. Speak with me again when you are ready.","rew":"Money: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 1,050\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"‹name›, you return. Do you have our supplies from the Undercity?","done":"Good work, ‹name›. These weapons will ensure our Deathguards don't get caught unprepared.\nYou have done a valuable service for our Dark Lady.\nUndercity Silverpine Forest","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":63.3,"y":48.6,"n":"Michael Garrett","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":43.4,"y":41.7,"n":"Deathguard Podrig","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"1364":{"id":1364,"t":"Mazen's Behest","lv":41,"min":37,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve Khadgar's Essays on Dimensional Convergence and deliver them to Watcher Mahar Ba in Nethergarde Keep.\nKhadgar's Essays on Dimensional Convergence Mire Lord 5 % , Tangled Horror 5 % , Swampwalker Elder 5 % , Swampwalker 5 %","desc":"Master Mazen's directions were quite clear: Deliver a very important essay to Watcher Mahar Ba in Nethergarde Keep.\nBut I had never been to the Blasted Lands before! The journey was frightening!\nWhen I got to the Swamp of Sorrows, I made a wrong turn and ended up surrounded by horrible plant-like swamp creatures. They lurched as if to attack me so I ran. But in my haste I dropped the essay. One of the beasts took it I am sure.\nCould you please try to retrieve it and deliver it to Mahar Ba?","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nTeacher's Sash Wanderlust Boots\nExperience: 3,300\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"What brings you to Nethergarde Keep, ‹race›?","done":"Ah, most splendid!\nFor some time I had feared my request for Khadgar's Essays on Dimensional Convergence had been overlooked by Master Mazen of the Academy of Arcane Arts and Sciences.\nHe must be bogged down with requests considering the many strange happenings going on.\nNow, if you'll excuse me, I need to begin my research at once. To finally glimpse the insight of one as great as Khadgar excites me to no end.\nStormwind City Blasted Lands Swamp of Sorrows","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":51.4,"y":73.8,"n":"Acolyte Dellis","s":1},{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":67.6,"y":19.2,"n":"Watcher Mahar Ba","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"3444":{"id":3444,"t":"The Stone Circle","lv":51,"min":46,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 4,900 experience instead of 4,700, 1.04 times as much.","obj":"Retrieve the Stone Circle from Marvon Rivetseeker's workshop in Ratchet.\nStone Circle Marvon's Chest","desc":"I once entered the foreboding chambers of the Sunken Temple. The evil in that place penetrates all that enter; I barely managed to find my way out, wading through the ooze that now covers the floors. All I can remember is stumbling through a large circular room, filled with serpent statues...\nRecently, I discovered a round stone that appeared to have the same serpent symbol imprinted on it. I had it packed up and shipped to my workshop in Ratchet. Retrieve it, and I might be able to tell you more.","rew":"Experience: 4,900","back":"Ratchet is not far from here, ‹name›. The journey shouldn't take long.","done":"Yes... This is the stone.\nIt's all coming back to me now, ‹name›...","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.7,"y":45.9,"n":"Marvon Rivetseeker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"3924":{"id":3924,"t":"Samophlange Manual","lv":19,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Samophlange Manual to Rilli Greasygob in Orgrimmar.\nSamophlange Manual","desc":"I think I can fix the samophlange, but I'm going to need the user's manual first. When I was in the Venture Company I had a rival, Boss Copperplug, who hoarded the secrets of the samophlange, giving out small bits of knowledge on the device to those he trusted. I wasn't one of the trusted few...\nBoss Copperplug used to stay at the Boulder Lode Mine in northeastern Barrens. Get the manual from him, and if he's given pages from it to anyone, you'll have to collect them too.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nTork Wrench Samophlange Screwdriver\nExperience: 1,800\n+150 reputation with Ratchet\n+75 reputation with Horde","back":"Do you have the manual?","done":"You got the manual! I can't wait to read it and find out how to fix the Samophlange! I spoke with Sputtervalve in Ratchet--he wanted to thank you for your help, and wanted to reward your efforts.\nI want to thank you too, and if I ever get this thing fixed I'll let you know...\nOrgrimmar The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":76.5,"y":24.4,"n":"Rilli Greasygob","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"5044":{"id":5044,"t":"Wisdom of Agamaggan","lv":20,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"4 Blood Shard Bristleback Geomancer 49 % , Bristleback Thornweaver 48.8 % , Bristleback Water Seeker 48.7 % , Bristleback Hunter 34 % and 4 more","rew":"You will learn: Wisdom of Agamaggan","back":"The shaman and geomancers of the quilboar tribes <snort> call upon the strength of Agamaggan to help them in battle and in their rituals, ‹race›.\nIf you too wish the added power of Agamaggan's blessing with your spells, then bring me 4 blood shards and Mangletooth will aid you. <snort>","done":"Your enemies should fear you even more, ‹race›. <snort>\nTell Mangletooth tales of your cunning in battle when next we meet--be it in this life, or the next. <snort>","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.5,"y":59.3,"n":"Mangletooth","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"884":{"id":884,"t":"Owatanka","lv":24,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Owatanka's Tailspike to Jorn at Camp Taurajo.\nOwatanka's Tailspike Owatanka\nProvided: Owatanka's Tailspike","desc":"When touched, sparks fly from the tailspike of Owatanka.","rew":"Experience: 1,450\n+75 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"‹name›, there is a new power behind your eyes! You have met with the mighty Owatanka, have you not?","done":"The thunder lizard Owatanka is called Bluebolt by the tauren, for within him resides a speed that belies his size. It is said that lightning struck Bluebolt long ago and, fed from the sky's rage, the great beast's energy is without limit.\nMay his energy flow through you, ‹name›. For you now keep pace with Owatanka.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.9,"y":59.1,"n":"Jorn Skyseer","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"1444":{"id":1444,"t":"Return to Fel'Zerul","lv":44,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Fel'Zerul in Stonard.","desc":"Jammal'an the Prophet sentenced me to exile from The Temple of Atal'Hakkar. I once felt the high priest was a worthy leader.\nHis unyielding faith in his prophecy will bring about the destruction of the Atal'ai. If it hasn't already.\nWhen I expressed my concerns, I was labeled an infidel and ousted from the temple.\nThose artifacts you brought to me are harmless. But if Jammal'an has found the proper fetish enchantment for the summoning ritual, the world lies in great peril....","rew":"Experience: 3,750\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"It has been quite some time since we spoke, ‹class›. I hope your journey was successful.\nWhat knowledge did you gain from the exiled Atal'ai in the Hinterlands?\nThe Hinterlands Swamp of Sorrows","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":33.8,"y":75.2,"n":"Atal'ai Exile","s":1},{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":47.9,"y":54.8,"n":"Fel'zerul","e":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"7844":{"id":7844,"t":"Cannibalistic Cousins","lv":48,"min":44,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Mystic Yayo'jin at Revantusk Village in the Hinterlands wants you to kill 30 Vilebranch Scalpers and 15 Vilebranch Soothsayers. Return to her when this task is complete.\nYayo'jin indicated that these trolls could be found near the Shaol'watha and Agol'watha temples in the north by northeastern region of the Hinterlands.\nVilebranch Scalper slain : 0/ 30\nVilebranch Soothsayer slain : 0/ 15","desc":"Three different tribes of trolls inhabit the Hinterlands, ‹name›. That is about as far as the similarities between the tribes extends: We are all trolls and we live in the Hinterlands.\nThe Vilebranch - aptly named - are a depraved lot; feeding on other trolls and humanoids.\nIf Zul'jin were here, he would have destroyed the whole lot of them with a flick of his wrist - alas, Zul'jin has not yet returned and we are left to our own devices.\nIt is up to you to destroy the filth of the region!","rew":"Money: 1 40 1 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Revantusk Trolls","back":"The Vilebranch Soothsayers and Scalpers inhabit the north by northeast region of the Hinterlands.","done":"Well done, ‹class›. Zul'jin himself could not have done a better job!","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":78.8,"y":78.2,"n":"Mystic Yayo'jin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"404":{"id":404,"t":"A Putrid Task","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 7 Putrid Claws to Deathguard Dillinger in Brill.\n7 Putrid Claw Ravaged Corpse 33 % , Rotting Dead 33 %","desc":"Scourge have trickled into Tirisfal Glades and have infested the area west of Brill, near the old bridge.\nGo there and beat back the rotting dead and ravaged corpses you find. Scatter their bones and bring back their putrid claws, and the Deathguards will reward you.","rew":"Money: 1 0 gold, 1 silver, 0 copper Experience: 410\n+75 reputation with Undercity","back":"Have you completed the task with which I have charged you? Do you have those putrid claws?","done":"Well done. I regret not being there to see you smash those undead into rotting pulp!","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":58.2,"y":51.4,"n":"Deathguard Dillinger","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"3844":{"id":3844,"t":"It's a Secret to Everybody","lv":52,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Look around in the pond for a clue about who this wrecked raft may belong to.","desc":"A destroyed raft rests along the shoreline. Considering this is only a small pond, it is not clear as to how it ended up here, although looking at the trees tells you that the water level may not be constant.\nPerhaps a little exploration in the area might uncover more clues...","rew":"Experience: 1,250","done":"A water-logged pack rests at the bottom of the pond.","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":63,"y":68.6,"n":"A Wrecked Raft","s":1},{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":63.1,"y":69.1,"n":"A Small Pack","e":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"4244":{"id":4244,"t":"Chasing A-Me 01","lv":53,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find a Mithril Casing and return to A-Me 01 in Un'Goro Crater.\nMithril Casing Stormpike Shredder Unit 19 % , 7:XT 12.1 % , Frostwolf Shredder Unit 8 % , Clunk 4 %","desc":"A little further investigation shows a panel that slides open. Clearly written above some wiring is the statement, \"Replace Mithril Casing And Turn Power Off Then On.\"\nTaking a moment to replace the panel, you wonder if it'll be that simple to fix A-Me 01 and get her back to Karna Remtravel near Marshall's Refuge.\nOnly trying it will tell.","rew":"Experience: 3,950","back":"The panel in which the mithril casing goes is still closed shut. The rest of A-Me 01 remains inert.","done":"You remove the panel from A-Me 01's back yet again and carefully remove the old mithril casing that seems to have burnt out. The new one slides into place easily. The only thing left to do, assuming the mithril casing was the problem, is to flip the switch to the \"Off\" position, and then back to the \"On\" position.","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":67.7,"y":16.8,"n":"A-Me 01","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"4084":{"id":4084,"t":"Silver Heart","lv":54,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 54 instead of 55.","obj":"Collect 11 Silvery Claws and 1 Irontree Heart for Eridan Bluewind in Felwood.\n11 Silvery Claws Angerclaw Mauler 45 % , Angerclaw Grizzly 45 % , Angerclaw Bear 45 % , Mongress 45 % and 4 more\nIrontree Heart Irontree Stomper 45 % , Irontree Wanderer 45 %","desc":"I do not know the one you speak of, ‹name›.\nBut worry not; if your friend was on a journey to find me, I do know what it was he desired.\nIn the heart of Un'Goro Crater dwells evil of the purest form. This evil takes the shape of an elemental called Blazerunner... protected by an aura that none can dispel...\nNone... except those with enough power to do so. I can teach you of this power, ‹name›.\nFirst, do as I ask. Collect 11 Silvery Claws and 1 Irontree Heart from the creatures in Felwood, then return.","rew":"Experience: 5,450","back":"I can tell you more of the power required to defeat Blazerunner, but first, you need to gather the things I require.","done":"Very well, ‹name›. I can see you are serious about helping your friend.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":51.3,"y":81.5,"n":"Eridan Bluewind","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"65604":{"id":65604,"t":"The binding","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Using the Withered Scarf, summon and subdue an incubus, then return the Withered Scarf to Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar.\nSummoned Incubus slain\nProvided: Withered Scarf","desc":"Yes... I see. I feel the residual emotions bound within these threads. Love is woven into its stitches. The incubus will not be able to resist.\nTake this to the summoning circle in Neeru's tent, ‹name›. Summon forth a malevolent incubus, then show it your mastery. Do not expect it to be subdued quietly. Ready your magic and prepare yourself for a fight. Underestimating a demon has been many a warlock's final mistake.\nWhen you have defeated it, return the cloth to me. I will let Magar know what you found.","rew":"You will receive:\nSmall Soul Pouch\nExperience: 1,150","back":"The sayaad are dominators of minds and torturers of souls. Their visage brings the heart joy, leaving you defenseless when they rend your flesh with whip and claw.\nDo not entertain the incubus' charms, ‹name›. Slay it quickly and let it be done.","done":"Hah! Victorious, as expected!\nThe incubus is subdued, and it will be my pleasure to teach you to summon the demon. You strength is growing, and I have no doubt that this is a mere stepping stone to even greater powers.\nI will return the scarf to Magar. I have known that orc for many years, and never did I think he would care for someone the way he cared for Krilge.\nIt is a reminder of what separates us from the demons. We wield their darkness, but they will never wield us.\nOrgrimmar Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":48.2,"y":45.6,"n":"Gan'rul Bloodeye","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"4964":{"id":4964,"t":"The Completed Orb of Dar'Orahil","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Wait for Menara Voidrender to complete the Orb of Dar'Orahil and then speak to her again.","desc":"I will get started immediately on crafting your orb and infusing your new demon into it. When done, you will have the choice of having it in the form of a staff or orb. I always felt it was important to cater to a warlock's chosen weapon... I see no reason not to continue that practice.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nOrb of Dar'Orahil Staff of Dar'Orahil\nExperience: 3,900","done":"It is done, ‹name›. Simply tell me which you'd prefer: a staff that would require you to use both hands, or an orb so you may use a dagger or sword as your weapon.\nTackling a felhound was a great feat on your part. I am sure your item will serve you well in the future. Continue to work hard in the arts, ‹name›. I will be awaiting details of your exploits.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.5,"y":35.4,"n":"Menara Voidrender","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1684":{"id":1684,"t":"Elanaria","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Elanaria.","desc":"Greetings, warrior. Your skill grows, but there is more to your profession than you may believe. To further progress, you must soon find a teacher.\nThe warrior Elanaria dwells in Darnassus, at the Warrior's Terrace. She can instruct you.","rew":"Experience: 85","done":"I bid you greetings, ‹name›. Your name rings loudly in Darnassus, for you show promise. But we shall soon see if you possess the strength of will to follow the path of the warrior.\nTeldrassil Darkshore Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":54.6,"y":58.5,"n":"Moon Priestess Amara","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.2,"y":59.2,"n":"Kyra Windblade","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":39,"y":43.6,"n":"Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":57.3,"y":34.6,"n":"Elanaria","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"1844":{"id":1844,"t":"Chimaeric Horn","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Galvanized Horn to Orm Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff.\nGalvanized Horn Chimaera Matriarch 80 %","desc":"I will make you the helm, but you must show me you are worthy of it.\nNestled in the northwestern reaches of the Stonetalon Mountains there lies the Charred Vale. It was once a verdant place, but is now defiled and ashen, and what creatures remain there are mad with pain and despair.\nThat place is where I send you, ‹name›.\nYou must go to the Charred Vale and find a chimaera matriarch. Slay her, free her of her misery. Bring me her galvanized horn as proof, and I shall make for you the helm.","rew":"Experience: 1,200","back":"Do you have the horn? Is the matriarch free of pain?","done":"You have completed your task, ‹name›, and shown me your worth and resolve. The helm will be yours...","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":39,"y":56,"n":"Orm Stonehoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"8404":{"id":8404,"t":"Fight for Warsong Gulch","lv":29,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Warsong Gulch Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The Silverwing Sentinels are at war with the Warsong Outriders due to the destruction the Orcs are causing to the forest. There are, however, more reasons to defend this particular forest than plain love for nature.\nThe forest forms a strategic barrier that makes Ashenvale defendable against a large-scale attack. Without it, Astranaar would last a day or two before being annexed to the Barrens.\nDo your part in fighting the Warsong Outriders, ‹name›! For the Alliance!","rew":"Experience: 1,200\n+50 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels","back":"You've come back with news from the front, ‹name›?","done":"Good work, ‹name›. Thanks to you, our natural defenses in Ashenvale will remain intact for another day.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"6004":{"id":6004,"t":"Unfinished Business","lv":56,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 2 Scarlet Medics, 2 Scarlet Hunters, 2 Scarlet Magi and 2 Scarlet Knights before returning to Kirsta Deepshadow in Western Plaguelands.\nScarlet Medic slain : 0/ 2\nScarlet Hunter slain : 0/ 2\nScarlet Mage slain : 0/ 2\nScarlet Knight slain : 0/ 2","desc":"I was sent as a scout to do some damage and gauge the strength of Hearthglen's defenses. Some people in the Alliance feel the little town has more than historical importance. It's not my job to question what that importance is, but regardless, I'm in no shape to continue until I rest up.\nIf you're willing, I'd pay handsomely for some help. Start south of here at their camp near the small bulwark they've set up. If you prove strong enough, maybe I could get your help with my main goal.","rew":"Money: 65 0 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,800","back":"How is it going, ‹name›? Are they stronger than you thought? I hope not. If I'm going to follow through here, then it's going to require a heck of a lot more strength than what I've already asked you to do.","done":"Well done, ‹name›. I'm amazed you dealt with them so quickly. Thank you.\nI have yet to meet anyone that approves of the Scarlet Crusade and their methods. I believe in the Light as much as anyone else in Stormwind, but they've demonstrated that they only want to kill anyone not loyal to their movement... even innocents.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":51.9,"y":28.1,"n":"Kirsta Deepshadow","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"964":{"id":964,"t":"Skeletal Fragments","lv":57,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 15 Skeletal Fragments to Apothecary Dithers at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.\n15 Skeletal Fragments Skeletal Terror 80 % , Skeletal Acolyte 80 % , Skeletal Warlord 80 % , Skeletal Executioner 80 % and 2 more","desc":"The key to Scholomance is called a Skeleton Key. It must be forged from the remains of a skeleton - several actually - and hardened by only the strongest of metals within a suitable mold. A signet of power from a being who naturally can open the portal to Scholomance will make the key ultimately function.\nFirst thing's first though, ‹name›. We'll need skeletal fragments for the key's forging. Skeletons inside Andorhal should yield what we need, but the ones outside the walls might work too.","rew":"Experience: 4,500","back":"Kill many and kill often, ‹class› - we'll need a decent supply of suitable skeletal fragments to make up the outer layer of the key. They don't call it a Skeleton Key for nothing, you know.","done":"This'll work, ‹name›! My turn now - I will imbue these with a suitable temper that will allow them to survive the intense forging process they will eventually go through.\nThe next step will be to get an appropriate mold for the key. I know a goblin blacksmith in Tanaris that has in the past made molds for similarly macabre items. He works for whom goblins usually work for - the highest bidder.\nTirisfal Glades Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.3,"y":69.2,"n":"Apothecary Dithers","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5524":{"id":5524,"t":"Chromatic Mantle of the Dawn","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 25 Argent Dawn Valor Tokens to Quartermaster Hasana at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.\n25 Argent Dawn Valor Token\nReach 42000 reputation with Argent Dawn","desc":"Brother/Sister ‹name› - your deeds on behalf of the Argent Dawn are far too numerous to be recounted easily. As a fitting tribute, I'll part with one of our special Chromatic Mantles of the Dawn - a version that protects the wearer from all forms of resistible magic simultaneously. Chromatic Mantles of the Dawn are reserved for only the mightiest of the Dawn's heroes!\nBring to me twenty-five valor tokens as a sign of tribute, and I'll give you the finest of all our mantles.","rew":"You will receive:\nChromatic Mantle of the Dawn\nExperience: 8,300\n+150 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Salutations, mighty ‹class›! Have you brought the valor tokens I asked of you? Once you hand them to me, I will issue you your own Chromatic Mantle of the Dawn.","done":"Most impressive, ‹name› - the Chromatic Mantle of the Dawn is now yours!\nAs long as you maintain Exalted status with the Argent Dawn, you will be able to purchase additional Chromatic Mantles. They will be made available to you immediately from any of the Dawn's quartermasters.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.3,"y":68.1,"n":"Argent Quartermaster Hasana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"484":{"id":484,"t":"Young Crocolisk Skins","lv":22,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Obtain 6 Young Crocolisk Skins for James Halloran in Menethil Harbor.\n6 Young Crocolisk Skin","desc":"I'm James Halloran, the tanner. My cured crocolisk skins are sought after all over, shipments leaving by boat to ports around the world.\nMet Einar? He's one of the hunters that brings crocolisk skins in for me.\nI'm a bit short on the softer skins that come off crocolisk young.\nBeing that I'm running low, I'll pay you top coin for a stack of the skins. You can find the young crocs in the waters right outside of town.","rew":"Money: 14 0 gold, 14 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,750\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"‹name›, right? Do you have my skins?","done":"Nice work you've done here, ‹name›. The quality of these skins is superb. I'll have to get them into the curing process as soon as possible. Oh, but before I get to that, there's some other work I need done that I think you might be able to take care of.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":8.5,"y":55.7,"n":"James Halloran","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"4804":{"id":4804,"t":"Chillwind E'ko","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"3 Chillwind E'ko Chillwind Ravager 2.7 % , Chillwind Chimaera 2.2 % , Fledgling Chillwind 1.3 %","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Juju Chill","back":"In Winterspring, you will fight great flying creatures called da Chillwind. These beasts possess da power ta wield frost magics. If you wish ta gain resistance ta frost, bring me da E'ko you find from da Chillwind.\nRememba, you must have the Cache of Mau'ari in your inventory if you want ta hunt for E'ko.","done":"Mau'ari can derive da juju for ‹name›... Use da Cache of Mau'ari to cast dis upon yourself or your allies.","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Witch Doctor Mau'ari","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"5124":{"id":5124,"t":"Fiery Plate Gauntlets","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Malyfous Darkhammer 6 Enchanted Thorium Bars, 2 Essence of Fire, and 4 Star Rubies. You will also need to turn in your Unfired Plate Gauntlets.\nUnfired Plate Gauntlets Unfired Plate Gauntlets\n6 Enchanted Thorium Bar\n2 Essence of Fire Baron Charr 75.2 % , Prince Skaldrenox 59.2 % , Baron Geddon 50 % , Ragnaros 40 % and 4 more\n4 Star Ruby Scholomance Student 7.7 % in Scholomance , Doomguard Commander 6.7 % , Dreamroarer 6.1 % , Living Storm 5.6 % and 4 more","desc":"By Thaurissan's beard!\nWhere did you find them?\nMore importantly, are you willing to part with them? Naturally, I would pay you for such a noble gesture.\nI'll tell you what, ‹name›. If you give me those unfired gauntlets, I will teach you how to make a set all your own. All you need to do is collect the parts for me so that I may narrow down the exact recipe.\nDo we have a deal??\nHere's the list of what I need, I'll front the non-enchanted thorium myself since you're supplying the gauntlets.","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Fiery Plate Gauntlets Fiery Plate Gauntlets\nExperience: 8,300","back":"Time is money, ‹name› and I don't have much of either.","done":"As promised, ‹name›, here's your recipe! I'm also going to throw in a little something extra for all of your hard work and dedication. What am I going to do with these anyway???","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61,"y":38.8,"n":"Malyfous Darkhammer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"92644":{"id":92644,"t":"Unfortunate news","lv":11,"min":6,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver the glowing crystal to Talanaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.\nProvided: Glowing Crystal","desc":"<You reach beneath the still-warm body of the turncoat cultist and recover a small, glowing blue crystal. It appears to be damaged, but it may still be important. High Elder Shadowsong may be interested in this.>","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nTracker's Pants Elder's Tunic Peacekeeper's Mail\nExperience: 440\n+10 reputation with Windshapers\n+10 reputation with High Order","back":"You are back? And... alone?","done":"The turncoat was already dead when you arrived, you say? This is unfortunate news.\n<You hand over the crystal you found on the dead cultist's body.>\nInteresting...","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":56,"y":58.8,"n":"Dead Cultist","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":76.6,"n":"Talaanis Shadowsong","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"94484":{"id":94484,"t":"Unnerving silence","lv":11,"min":8,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find and speak with Elegael Thornpaw in the northeastern part of Shadowgale Forest.","desc":"A moment, if you will ‹name›. Are you headed towards Shadowgale Forest? There is a druid conclave there in a cave to the northeast. I have been waiting on word from them but their correspondence is long overdue.\nWith Ban'aethall in ruins and all the unrest lately I worry something dire may have happened. Please, if you are able go, seek out Elegael Thornpaw and put my mind at ease.","done":"Thank goodness our message got to Lotheluum. Wait, where are the rest of the reinforcements? Surely it is not just you they sent?\n<Elegael pales as you relay your conversation with Lotheluum.>\nSo the message did not get through. We are in dire straights indeed then.\nIt seems we must handle this on our own. Time is of the essence.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":64,"y":75,"n":"Lotheluum Starbreeze","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":61.6,"y":39.2,"n":"Elegael Thornpaw","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});